262
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:27,520
When you launch, you have an influx of new customers.

263
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:32,160
Those customers by definition are very, very early in their life cycle.

264
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:35,520
Early users churn at higher rates than older users.

265
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:36,240
It makes sense.

266
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:40,160
If you see value, you stay around and you're less likely to churn over time.

267
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,160
If you don't see value, you leave early.

268
00:22:42,800 --> 00:22:54,080
And so comparing a business that is in the first month of launch to a business that's like 15 years old and the majority of its subscriber base is older than 10 years is just a complete apples to oranges comparison.

